<article class="app-prose">
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
        Mythos Log treats real habits like character training. You log effort against your skills, build stats over time, and a weekly review decides what levels up.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
        Email: <a href="{{ apps.supportEmailUrl }}">{{ apps.supportEmail }}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Before Contacting Support</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Restart the app.</li>
        <li>Ensure iCloud is enabled.</li>
        <li>Update to latest version.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>How do weekly reviews work?</strong> Progress, stagnation, decay and level-ups are resolved once a week in the Weekly Review.</li>
        <li><strong>How do I connect Apple Health?</strong> Turn on workout import in the app’s Settings and allow access when prompted. You can change this later in the Health settings.</li>
        <li><strong>Why aren’t my workouts importing?</strong> Check that Mythos Log has Health access in Settings &gt; Health &gt; Data Access &amp; Devices &gt; Mythos Log. Only eligible Strength and Cardio workouts are imported.</li>
        <li><strong>How do I sync between iPhone and iPad?</strong> Sign in to the same iCloud account on both devices and make sure iCloud is enabled for Mythos Log.</li>
        <li><strong>How do I back up or move my data?</strong> Use Export in the app’s Settings to save your data to a file you choose.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Deleting Data</h2>
    <p>
        Delete the app to remove the data stored on your device. To remove synced data, go to Settings &gt; [your name] &gt; iCloud &gt; Manage Storage &gt; Mythos Log. Removing Mythos Log’s access in Settings &gt; Health &gt; Data Access &amp; Devices stops workout reading and does not delete anything from Apple Health.
    </p>

    <h2>Response Time</h2>
    <p>
        We aim to respond within a few days.
    </p>
</article>
